# Vocabulary and Neural Networks in the Computational Assessment of Texts Written by Second-Language Learners.

**Authors:** Meara, Paul, Rodgers, Catherine, Jacobs, Gabriel

## Abstract
Explores the potential of a neural network in language assessment. Nonnative speakers of French were asked to produce a short text in response to a picture stimulus. A neural network was trained to grade the text on the basis of codings. Results suggest that it may be possible to teach a neural network to mimic the judgments made by human markers. (Author/VWL)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ613078

